  "question": {
    "text": "A bag contains&nbsp;<math><mn>21</mn></math> markers with numbers&nbsp;<math><mn>1</mn></math> to <math><mn>21</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;A marker is drawn at random and then replaced and then a second marker is drawn. The probability that the first number is odd and the second is even is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>110</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>441</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>441</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Probability that the first marker is odd <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Probability that the second marker is even <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />The required probability <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>110</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>441</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
